Change Backout Plan

Estimated Backout Duration: 30–60 minutes

Backout Steps
Log in to the Azure Portal using an account with Network Contributor or equivalent permissions.
Identify all Network Security Groups (NSGs) updated during the implementation.
For each affected NSG:
Navigate to Networking → Network Security Groups.
Open the Inbound Security Rules section.
Delete the Base_Deny rule (Priority: 4096).
Save the changes.
Repeat the same process under Outbound Security Rules and remove the Base_Deny rule.
Verify that the NSG configuration has reverted to its previous state.
Perform connectivity validation to ensure application traffic is restored to the pre-change state.
Update the ServiceNow Change Request with the rollback activities, validation results, and completion status.

Backout Success Criteria

Base_Deny rule has been removed from all affected NSGs.
Existing NSG rules remain unchanged.
Application and network connectivity is restored to the pre-change state.
No unexpected Azure activity or connectivity issues are observed.
Validation Plan

Validation Duration: Approximately 30 minutes

Validation Activities
Verify that the Base_Deny rule has been successfully added to both Inbound and Outbound security rules for every NSG listed in the customer spreadsheet.
Confirm the rule configuration matches the approved implementation:
Rule Name: Base_Deny
Priority: 4096
Access: Deny
Protocol: Any (*)
Source: Any (*)
Destination: Any (*)
Confirm all existing NSG rules remain unchanged and retain their original priorities.
Validate that existing application traffic continues to function as expected by performing connectivity tests from representative source systems.
Verify there are no unexpected connectivity failures or blocked business traffic after implementation.
Review Azure Activity Logs (if required) to confirm successful rule creation.
Obtain customer confirmation (if applicable) that services remain operational.
Record validation results in the Change Request and mark the implementation as successful.

Validation Success Criteria

Base_Deny rule is present on all targeted NSGs.
Rule priority is 4096.
Existing higher-priority allow/deny rules are unchanged.
Business applications remain accessible.
No production incidents or unexpected alerts are generated following the change.
